The [#4471 incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug, one fix. The reports say otherwise.
Ticket #4471 holds three different problems. Fixing the parser closes only the first.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Merging by subject line (<a href="/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject">decision 0001</a>)
put reports with different causes into one ticket. The parser fix will not close the other two.
</Callout>

## The three problems

<ProblemCounts ticket={4471} />

1. **Parser reads dates month first.** Tenants that write the day first see day and month
   swapped. This is the bug the desk already knew about. It covers most of the reports.
2. **The booking-v3 form hint says `MM/DD/YYYY`.** The form tells people to type the month
   first, and the tenant then reads it day first. The parser fix does not touch this: the
   hint text and the form need their own change. These reports all arrived through the form.
3. **A date moves by one day.** The month is right and the day is off by one. Clues in the
   reports point to time zones (one meeting, two cities, two days; an invite that arrived
   before the booking). Nobody has confirmed the cause. It needs its own investigation.

## How the reports were sorted

- **One id, one report.** The ticket system exports in overlapping pages, so the same report
  can come twice. The counts use each id once.
- **The tenant decides the cause, not intake.** `intakeTag` is a guess made from the
  reporter's browser. The tenant's locale and booking form say which bug it was.
- **The body decides the one-day reports.** The desk read five reports as a one-day move.
  By tenant they would be filed under the parser, but they do not describe a swap.

The desk's own table groups by tenant only. It files the five one-day reports under the
parser, so it shows 379 there. Take the five out and the parser count is the 374 above.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What to do

- Keep the parser fix on its ticket, and count only the swap reports against it.
- Open a separate ticket for the booking-v3 form hint.
- Open a separate ticket for the one-day move, and ask for more detail from the five reporters.
- When the desk merges, look at the tenant and the channel as well as the subject line.

